    <rdfs:comment>Inverse of usesConcept: this concept/operation is used by the given method, construct, or built-in function.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#op_search">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#Concept"/>
    <rdfs:label>Search/Count (operation)</rdfs:label>
    <difficulty rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">low</difficulty>
    <socraticQuestion>Besides looping yourself, what questions can you ask about whether a value is present?</socraticQuestion>
    <sharedConcept rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</sharedConcept>
    <canonicalId>core:op_search</canonicalId>
    <onPath rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</onPath>
    <definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Abstract operation: find whether / where a value occurs in a collection.</definition>
    <cognitiveType rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">understand</cognitiveType>
    <taughtIn rdf:resource="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#W5_lists"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#implementedBy">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#Concept"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#ConceptCarrier"/>
    <rdfs:label>implementedBy</rdfs:label>
    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#implementsConcept"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Inverse of implementsConcept: a concept is coded by this language construct, method, or built-in.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#isMutable">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#DataType"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
    <rdfs:label>isMutable</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Whether the type can be changed in place after creation.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#list_comprehension">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#Concept"/>
    <rdfs:label>List Comprehension</rdfs:label>
    <difficulty rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">high</difficulty>
    <socraticQuestion>Can you build this new list in one line instead of a for loop?</socraticQuestion>
    <onPath rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</onPath>
    <definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A concise syntax that always builds a new list; it does not mutate an existing list.</definition>
    <cognitiveType rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">apply</cognitiveType>
    <taughtIn rdf:resource="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#W5_lists"/>
    <dependsOn rdf:resource="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#iteration"/>
    <dependsOn rdf:resource="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#for_loop"/>
    <dependsOn rdf:resource="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#list"/>
    <confusedWith rdf:resource="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#for_loop"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#for_loop">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#LanguageConstruct"/>
    <rdfs:label>for loop</rdfs:label>
    <difficulty rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">low</difficulty>
    <onPath rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</onPath>
    <definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Syntax that iterates over an iterable, binding each element in turn.</definition>
    <cognitiveType rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">apply</cognitiveType>
    <taughtIn rdf:resource="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#W3_control"/>
    <revisitedIn rdf:resource="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#W5_lists"/>
    <implementsConcept rdf:resource="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#iteration"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#collection">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#Concept"/>
    <rdfs:label>Collection</rdfs:label>
    <difficulty rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">low</difficulty>
    <socraticQuestion>If you need several values to travel together as one group, what idea is that — before we care about order or labels?</socraticQuestion>
    <sharedConcept rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</sharedConcept>
    <canonicalId>core:collection</canonicalId>
    <onPath rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</onPath>
    <definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A grouping of elements treated as one whole (later specialized into sequences, sets, mappings).</definition>
    <cognitiveType rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">understand</cognitiveType>
    <taughtIn rdf:resource="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#W5_lists"/>
    <dependsOn rdf:resource="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#iterable"/>
    <dependsOn rdf:resource="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#element"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#recommendedBefore">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
    <rdfs:label>recommendedBefore</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Soft order among sibling peers when PATH / dependsOn do not already decide which to introduce first (a teaching dilemma). NOT the tutor spine — that total order is only in comp101_path_w5_w6.json (/path/next). Do not sprinkle on every consecutive PATH pair; skip when traversal order is already determined. Distinct from dependsOn (strict readiness) and confusedWith (student mix-ups).</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
