  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology"/>
    <owl:versionInfo>2025.36</owl:versionInfo>
    <rdfs:label>COMP101 course ontology</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Static curriculum ontology for the COMP101 intro programming course: lectures, concepts, Python data types, methods, errors, and skills. Cross-cutting concepts are tagged shared for merge with other course modules. Student misconceptions, symptoms, remediations, and evidence are modelled separately in the dynamic ontology (http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101-dynamic), which imports this one and references these ids. Pedagogy metadata (definition, cognitiveType, bestPractice) is populated incrementally on high-value targets; empty instances inherit schema from the OOP module for future merge. Engineering notes: AllDisjointClasses covers asserted leaf types (Lecture, Concept, DataType, ErrorType, LanguageConstruct, Method, BuiltInFunction, Skill); intermediate classes ConceptCarrier/Invokable and Pattern⊑Concept are organizational. Inverse object properties are declared for reasoners — A-Box asserts only the forward direction (taughtIn, dependsOn, …); apps must query forwards or expand inverses.</rdfs:comment>
    <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://gnosis.local/ontologies/comp101#list_reverse">
